    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21842" root="شحم" body-key="$">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَحِمٌ</span></b>  <i>Eagerly desirous of fat.</i> (S, K.) One
says, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَجُلٌ شَحِمٌ لَحِمٌ</span> <i>A man eagerly desirous of
fat and of flesh.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عِنَبٌ شَحِمٌ</span> <i>Grapes
having little juice</i> (K, TA) <i>and thick skin.</i> (TA.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُمَّانَةٌ شَحِمَةٌ</span> <i>A pomegranate having thick</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَحْمَة</span> [or <i>pulp amid the seeds</i>]. (TA.)

